WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.588
Feynman's letter to

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.213
his wife

00:00:02.742 --> 00:00:03.933
Abakcus tells the

00:00:03.744 --> 00:00:04.569
story of the

00:00:04.381 --> 00:00:05.760
letter Richard Feynman

00:00:05.584 --> 00:00:06.621
wrote to Arline

00:00:06.433 --> 00:00:07.459
sixteen months

00:00:07.542 --> 00:00:08.449
after her death

00:00:08.261 --> 00:00:09.805
in 1945

00:00:09.971 --> 00:00:11.173
which stayed sealed

00:00:10.985 --> 00:00:12.435
for forty-two years

00:00:12.958 --> 00:00:13.936
She died on

00:00:13.748 --> 00:00:16.012
June 16, 1945

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:17.097
a month before

00:00:16.908 --> 00:00:18.099
the Trinity test

00:00:18.238 --> 00:00:19.523
Richard Feynman is

00:00:19.335 --> 00:00:20.195
remembered for the

00:00:20.007 --> 00:00:20.808
things that can

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:21.363
be drawn on

00:00:21.175 --> 00:00:21.999
a blackboard

00:00:22.526 --> 00:00:23.776
Feynman married her

00:00:23.587 --> 00:00:24.212
anyway

00:00:24.283 --> 00:00:25.662
in 1942

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:27.148
against the protests

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.304
of both families

00:00:28.443 --> 00:00:29.598
The diagrams that

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:30.435
carry his name

00:00:30.247 --> 00:00:31.532
turned pages of

00:00:31.344 --> 00:00:32.558
brutal calculation

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:33.560
into little pictures

00:00:33.372 --> 00:00:34.751
of particles meeting

00:00:34.575 --> 00:00:35.471
and parting

00:00:36.006 --> 00:00:37.020
Full story on

00:00:36.831 --> 00:00:37.727
the dashboard
